      {
        "name": "repo-watcher",
        "summary": "Watch .git and refresh: the app now tracks external reality",
        "body": "The stale-status bug: the UI kept the state loaded at launch, so an\nism apply from a terminal left it showing files that no longer existed.\nA debounced fs.watch on the active project's .git pushes repo:changed;\nall git reads run with --no-optional-locks so our own refreshes never\ntrigger the watcher. Debouncer is unit-tested with fake timers.",
        "from": [
          "apps/desktop/src/main/services/watcher.test.ts:1#47e3",
          "apps/desktop/src/main/services/watcher.ts:1#fa6d"
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "fork-parity",
        "summary": "Model the client on Fork: staging, commit box, detail tabs",
        "body": "Modeled directly on Fork running side-by-side (closed source — its\ninteraction patterns, our implementation): icon toolbar with a repo/\nbranch card and Stash; sidebar with pinned views, a filter field and\ncollapsible Branches/Remotes/Tags/Stashes/Submodules (refs now carry\ntip shas for decorations); Local Changes with Unstaged/Staged areas,\nstage/unstage (git add / restore --staged), per-area diffs (--cached\nfor staged) and a subject/description/amend commit box that commits\nthe staged set; All Commits with a graph rail, branch/tag badges and\na Commit / Changes / File Tree detail panel (collapsed-chain file\ntree, unit-tested). Views land where the work is and refreshes never\nyank the selection or view.",
